{"name":"Golden Yarrow","hex":"#e2c74f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden yarrow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Eriophyllum confertiflorum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_yarrow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eriophyllum confertiflorum","blocks":[{"text":"Eriophyllum confertiflorum, commonly called golden yarrow or yellow yarrow, is a North American species of plant in the family Asteraceae, native to California and Baja California. It has wooly leaves when young, and yellow flower heads. \"Eriophyllum\" means \"wooly leaved.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Eriophyllum_confertiflorum_2004-04-07.jpg/330px-Eriophyllum_confertiflorum_2004-04-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eriophyllum_confertiflorum","wikidata":"Q5389476"},{"title":"Achillea millefolium","blocks":[{"text":"Achillea millefolium, commonly known as yarrow or common yarrow, is a flowering plant in the family Asteraceae. Growing to 1 metre tall, it is characterized by small whitish flowers, a tall stem of fernlike leaves, and a pungent odor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg/330px-Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achillea_millefolium","wikidata":"Q25408"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Eriophyllum_confertiflorum_yellow_yarrow